I have a few problems with this:

 spoilers sure to follow...
1) The Wizard of Yendor starts out around level 28 (!!!), and gains levels
   every time you "kill" him and he comes back.  At his level, he can hit
   most negative armor classes (down to about -20) fairly easily, so
   putting the "Random AC" clause makes it fair to the other monsters, but
   makes the Wizard hit you nearly constantly.  Add this to the fact that
   he can clone himself and summon hordes of other monsters to help.
   Tell me that it's too easy and no fun AFTER you've actually won.
   Most people can't even _get_ to the Wizard, and going back up is a lot
   tougher than the trip down.

2) It doesn't go both ways -- you don't get to strike at a modified
   negative armor class against monsters the way they can at you.

So has anyone actually won the real version of NH3.0?  If so, what
were your AC and primary weapon?

